            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0059" n="49" xml:id="pg49"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10568: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-02T19:00:00-03:00">May 2, 1941—7 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        10:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>395. My telegram No. 389, May 2, 2 p.m. I saw Nabuco again this evening. He said
                    that he had not yet sent the telegram to Madrid as he promised he would because
                    when he saw President Vargas this afternoon Vargas raised the question as to why
                    all of the Spanish-American Republics were not making an approach to the Spanish
                    Government on this. Vargas added that if all the Spanish-American countries with
                    diplomatic representatives in Spain were making representations to the Spanish
                    Government Brazil would be glad to join them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
